From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:40:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: leds: backlight: Describe the LM3534 behind
 Apple DWI

Document the I2C LED driver whose enable is controlled separately
from brightness on the DWI bus.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/leds/backlight/apple,dwi-bl.yaml        | 2 +-
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/trivial-devices.yaml          | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/backlight/apple,dwi-bl.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/backlight/apple,dwi-bl.yaml
index af1be17..7ee2f36 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/backlight/apple,dwi-bl.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/backlight/apple,dwi-bl.yaml
@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@ properties:
       The LED driver that receives the DWI brightness commands, when it has
       an enable of its own on another bus. A DWI brightness of 0 leaves its
       LEDs lit at their lowest current; they are only off while it is
-      disabled (iPad 5: TI LP8559 on I2C).
+      disabled (for example a TI LP8559 or LM3534 on I2C).
 
 required:
   - compatible
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/trivial-devices.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/trivial-devices.yaml
index d6d9762..d20e5b4 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/trivial-devices.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/trivial-devices.yaml
@@ -497,6 +497,8 @@ properties:
           - ti,hdc1050
             # Temperature and humidity sensor with i2c interface
           - ti,hdc1080
+            # LED driver with DWI brightness control
+          - ti,lm3534
             # Thermometer with SPI interface
           - ti,lm70
           - ti,lm71
